[Music]  honoring the lives lost on 9 11. tonight  the professional firefighters of nevada  hosted a memorial procession in downtown  las vegas the annual tribute only lasted  a couple of minutes but made a big  impact on those at the fremont  experience madison kimbrough joins us  live in the area tonight with the  details madison  21 years ago our country was bombarded  with tragedy but tonight las vegas came  together in remembrance  at that time the world just kind of  stopped  the fremont street experience looked a  lot different sunday evening as locals  tourists military and first responders  all gathered on maine and fremont for a  9 11 memorial procession the  professional fighter fighters of nevada  led the tribute procession in  partnership with the city of las vegas  those around recalling how impactful 9  11 was in their own lives many in  disbelief that it was actually 21 years  ago to the day i worked in the trade  center for 17 years we lost about 40  individuals i've also lost about  25 friends who are firemen history of it  will never change the  time passes but it still seemed caring  the effect on us  and then it's like since 9 11 the  craziness in the world is just gets more  bizarre and more bizarre after the march  there was a moment of silence followed  by a toast corey whitlock with the  professional fighter fighters of nevada  says having this annual event is a  reminder of the hard work first  responders go through on a regular basis  as these men and women every single day  step out to their fire stations put on  those bunker pants and go to these calls  and respond daily they feel that realism  and it's just a way that we can bring  our community together  the procession lasted about 15 minutes  and concluded here on third street in  collaboration with hogs and heifers bar  and downtown grand hotel and casino  reporting live in downtown las vegas  madison kimbrough 8 news now

